# The simulated MCU board (vt350#224): Kalico's AVR firmware for an atmega644p at 20 MHz, built for simulavr (no
# U2X baud), on UART0 (PD0/PD1, the pins platform/klipper/pinmap.py never gives out) at 250000 baud. Settings as
# Kalico's docs/Debugging.md "Testing with simulavr" and config/generic-simulavr.cfg. Every [mcu] in the printer's
# config runs its own copy of this one firmware, each in its own simulavr.
CONFIG_LOW_LEVEL_OPTIONS=y
CONFIG_MACH_AVR=y
CONFIG_MACH_atmega644p=y
CONFIG_AVR_FREQ_20000000=y
CONFIG_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_AVR_SERIAL_UART0=y
CONFIG_SIMULAVR=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_BAUD=250000
# Optional features a simulated board has no use for (no accelerometer, display, load cell, LED strip or
# thermocouple to talk to) are left out. That shrinks the data dictionary klippy reads at connect from 3462 to 2399
# bytes (zlib): simulavr runs far below real time, and klippy gives up on a connect after 5 s.
# A printer config using one of these gets an error at connect, naming the missing command.
# CONFIG_WANT_NEOPIXEL is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_PULSE_COUNTER is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_ST7920 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_HD44780 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_ADXL345 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_LIS2DW is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_MPU9250 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_ICM20948 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_THERMOCOUPLE is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_HX71X is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_ADS1220 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_ADS131M0X is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_CS1237 is not set
# CONFIG_WANT_LDC1612 is not set
